constructor for testing element in isolation Constructor associates \fBElement\fP with instance of specific finite element\&. This initialized the bridge pattern\&. Also, vectors of pointers to nodes, constraint points and neighbor elements are constructed\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
Finite element, for example \fBLinearTriangle\fP\&. The element type determines how many nodes and constraint points the \fBElement\fP will have and if affects the element dimensionality which can be queried with Dim()\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Elements are constructed inside the \fBMeshManager\fP\&. There are 2 methods for VSets and VSets respectively\&. VSets (a class that will be phased out in 1999) cannot hold different element types in one mesh\&. In this case the \fBElement\fP default constructor will initialize the \fBFiniteElement\fP reference to \fBFiniteElementManager\fP\&. In the case of VSets, specific element types can be stored and this constructor is used to reference them properly\&. 
