.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::Element\fP< dim >::Accept (\fBcsmp::Visitor\fP< dim > & vis)"
\fBVisitor\fP subclassed objects may be passed to the \fBElement\fP object to gain access to its public interface\&. This then allows the visitor to query the Elements methods for the data it needs for its own computations\&. Apart from just visiting each \fBElement\fP sequentially, a \fBVisitor\fP can target the Elements neigbor elements to which it simultaneously has access\&. This allows to implement a mesh traversal technique like streamline routing\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The visitor is queried for its application Target\&. Depending on the result it is applied to this \fBElement\fP or passed on to all of its Nodes, IntegrationPoints or Neighbors\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The Accept method is used, for instance, by the TranportVisitor class\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
