.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBcsmp::Node\fP< dim > *const \fBcsmp::Element\fP< dim >::N (uint32_t n) const"

.PP
accessor of the nodes of the current finite element The suite of methods Node(), \fBIntegrationPoint()\fP, Face() and \fBNeighbor()\fP, enables access of these connected objects via const references\&. A NULL pointer is returned by \fBNeighbor()\fP if the \fBElement\fP lies at the model boundary and a Neighbor does not exist\&. Also constraint points do not exist unless you defined these for the specific \fBFiniteElement\fP which you are using\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
An integer from 0\&.\&.\&.n-1, where n is the number of nodes per \fBElement\fP\&. Nodes are numbered clockwise for regular-gridded meshes (since Y points downward) and counter-clockwise for all other meshes\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
A range check is performed\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Use only when the other methods of the \fBElement\fP fail to give you enough information about the target object\&. For instance when you want to retrieve a \fBNode\fP coordinate:

.PP
.PP
.nf
double x = (*element\&.N(2))\->x();
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
return A pointer to the Target object, e\&.g\&. a \fBNode\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

