.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::Element\fP< dim >::NodeCoordinateMatrix (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & XY) const"

.PP
inputs node coordinates into supplied matrix Returns a matrix with 'nodes'-rows and 'coordinate-directions' columns\&. This Meschach++ matrix defines the positions of the elements nodes for the finite-element matrix assembly\&. Since the number of element nodes may vary among different elements types, the number of rows in XY may also vary from element to element\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIXY\fP A \fBDenseMatrix<DM_MIN>\fP class object (value type fT)\&. This matrix is dynamically resized if necessary but must have been constructed with a finite size before passing it to \fBCoordinateMatrix()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBElement\fP The node coordinates are returned into the supplied matrix\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Finite-element forms of differential equations require the global node coordinates of the element to calculate the element constribution to the global solution matrix\&. If the element uses local coordinates, the global node coordinates will still be required to compute Jacobian (coordinate- transformation) matrix\&. 
